Most important:
- Adjust wifi-manager/esp_app_main to at least contain two SSID's and two passwords. 
Also, the wificonnection is very unstable, so research is going to be necessary on how to solve this.
- Adjust squeezelite-ota/esp_app_main or related firmware to save the last type of flashed firmware (in this instance: tag I2S-4MFlash.16.1769.master-v4.3 and automatically pick up the next new release, when this drops.
So, filtering: I2S-4MFlash.*(>16.1769).master*(>-v4.3). Next step would be, a notification in my home assistant music assistant add-on/app.

Less important:
- in squeezelite some buffers (stream, output, header, recv) are allocated 
although they are almost static (expect output). This creates a risk of 
memory fragmentation, especially because the large output is re-allocated for
AirPlay
- libflac in lpc.c can be unrolled - that gains 43k of code, at the expense of 4% CPU